#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kweather; is an application that provides both a panel icon, allowing you "
"to watch the weather as reported by a local weather station, and providing a "
"weather service that can track multiple weather stations and provide this "
"information to other applications including &konqueror;'s navigation panel "
"and &kontact;'s summary page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kweather; as a Panel Applet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on an empty space in the panel and select <guimenuitem>Add "
"Applet to Panel...</guimenuitem> and then <guilabel>Weather Report</"
"guilabel> in the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A configuration dialog will open up. Initially the only configuration "
"required to make KWeather work is to select a weather station."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While the weather stations available are fairly comprehensive, not every "
"town in every country will be represented, simply because not every town has "
"an appropriate weather station. If your own town is not represented, you "
"should choose the one nearest you. Since flying planes safely requires "
"accurate weather data, most towns with an airport will be in the list, so a "
"good bet is to look for the nearest airport to you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At this point, you can press the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button and the "
"dialog will close. You will now have an icon displaying the current weather "
"graphically on your panel. Clicking it once will open a window that shows "
"the weather in detail."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Further configuration is described in the next chapter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kweather;"
msgstr ""

